{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/touring-exhibition/16","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe and Ansel Adams: Natural Affinities","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","id":"actor/1","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe and Ansel Adams: Natural Affinities brings together an important selection of these artists' paintings and photographs. The works date from the 1920s forward, and most significantly, they reveal the artists' ongoing deep attraction to and profound appreciation of the natural world. They take as their subjects the myriad of sizes, shapes, and textures of elements O'Keeffe and Adams found in their environments, from tiny flowers to the awesome vastness of wilderness areas.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"Activity"}